# Build-context filter for infra/deploy/engine/Dockerfile ONLY.
#
# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to a context-root
# .dockerignore, so this file scopes the exclusions to the preview engine image and
# leaves every other build (platform, the DDEV engine, the CI engine images) untouched.
# Patterns are relative to the build context, which is the repository root
# (infra/deploy/compose.yaml → engine.build.context).
#
# WHY. `COPY engine/ /app/engine/` copied the developer's host virtualenv into the
# served image: ~92MB of engine/.venv whose shebangs point at host paths and can never
# execute in the container, plus 178 __pycache__ directories built by another
# interpreter and a .pytest_cache. Measured 2026-08-17: 957MB before, 833MB after.
#
# engine/pyproject.toml is NOT excluded — it supplies `pythonpath` and the package
# metadata the running app depends on.

# Host virtualenv — never valid inside the image.
engine/.venv

# Host-built bytecode and pytest state. PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 keeps the container
# from creating its own.
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache

# Development surface: the black-box suite runs against the repository (infra/ci/engine
# gates bind-mount engine/), never from the served image, so it is inert weight and an
# unnecessary attack surface in a deployed container.
engine/tests
